Fix starter-catalog copy and expose its owner and readiness rules

Plain-words copy fixes and one shared search for the starter catalog. The suggested-tasks card's skip notice now reads 'will be skipped if you accept' instead of 'if you accept this interaction'. The 'What do you want done?' panel filters cards with the same searchStarterCards ranking the server search endpoint uses, mapped back onto the loaded card statuses in ranked order, so typing 'book' no longer surfaces the rebook card by substring while 'review' still finds the Google reviews card; an empty box shows everything. The panel's two blocker lines and the server's four operator-facing activation and refusal strings drop their em dashes for full stops and commas. A new StarterCatalogDialog test file (jsdom, createRoot, mocked starterCatalogApi and dialog shell) pins the shared ranking, proves typing and pressing Enter never activates a card, and checks the blocker copy; a server test statically scans the starter-catalog module with comments stripped and fails on any em or en dash in code or strings. Not touched but worth knowing: the shared catalog's daily-phone-report card prose still carries an em dash, which is outside this item's files.

The starter catalog's two internal rules are now standalone exported functions so the upcoming Start work planner can reuse them instead of keeping its own copies. blockersForPlugins(requiredKeys, state) is the single readiness check (a plugin must be installed and ready, otherwise it is reported as missing or switched off), pickAssigneeForCompany(db, companyId) is the single rule for who leads work (CEO, then an officer, then any agent that is not paused, terminated or still waiting for approval, or null) and now also returns the agent's name, and pluginStateByKey(db) reads the installed plugins. starterCatalogService keeps calling all three, so the seven starter cards behave exactly as before. Tests cover the readiness rule for every plugin status, the assignee order against an embedded Postgres database with four agents, that an agent still waiting for approval is never picked and leaves no lead at all when there is nobody else, that listForCompany's readiness equals the shared function's answer, and a structural check that the module holds only one copy of each rule.

The dialog files this item also touched are committed with the dialog change itself, so each file lands once.

